HONEST STATUS
-------------
Design / reference prototype. Unaudited. Pre-production. Not a certified
security product. NO real infrastructure is provisioned by this code — it is the
orchestration logic and the interfaces an operator's real provisioner plugs into.
The actual managed hosts are OPERATOR-RUN.

WHAT THIS IS / IS NOT
---------------------
- BUSINESS / ENTERPRISE ONLY. A managed node is provisioned only for a corporate
  TENANT holding a DUNS-backed master license (enterprise/licensing/). Personal
  Postern apps and personal data NEVER touch this control plane — there is no
  code path for it.
- HOSTED IS LESS PRIVATE THAN SELF-HOSTING. A managed node runs on infrastructure
  the org does not own, under a control plane the org does not run. We disclose
  this in the README and every user-facing surface; we never pitch it as "just as
  private" as running your own node. Self-hosting stays free.
- TENANT ISOLATION IS BY CONSTRUCTION — in-process namespacing, not a kernel or
  hypervisor boundary. A COMPROMISED CONTROL PLANE DEFEATS IT: whoever controls
  the orchestrator can read any tenant. We say so plainly.
- KEYED TO THE MASTER LICENSE. A tenant's nodes exist only while its master token
  verifies OFFLINE. Revoke or expiry ⇒ the tenant's nodes are deprovisioned and
  its namespace wiped. revoke ⇒ deprovision, fail-closed.
- NO TELEMETRY beyond the disclosed operational metrics (node counts, lifecycle
  state, provision/deprovision events, control-process uptime). No phone-home.
- This module implements NO cryptography and does NOT depend on the licensing
  library's code. The real offline verify() plugs in through a documented
  interface. The token generator lives on posternlabs.com.
- Payment (after evaluation) is FIAT; pricing is still being structured. Never a
  coin. The Bloch-SIS-PoW coin is not a security, not an asset, and buys no
  software.

The community/free personal suite is never "Postern OS"; Postern OS is the
separate reproducible operating system product.
